# DEV Firebase project (scriptally-dev) — environment for deployed Cloud Functions.
#
# firebase-tools loads functions/.env, then functions/.env.<projectId>, then
# functions/.env.<alias>, and merges them in that order (lib/functions/env.js, findEnvfiles).
# Named by projectId so it applies whether the deploy says `--project scriptally-dev` or
# `--project dev`. It carries no secret — secrets go through defineSecret/Secret Manager.
#
# ⚠️ `(default)` IS STATED EXPLICITLY AND IS NOT AN OMISSION. Dev's only Firestore database is
# `(default)`, so leaving this file out would also "work" — and that is precisely the problem it
# exists to remove. Explicit-and-correct and absent-and-lucky must be distinguishable, because on
# dev they produce identical behaviour and only one of them survives being copied to prod.
#
# ⚠️ IT CANNOT BE CALLED FIREBASE_DATABASE_ID. firebase-tools reserves the `FIREBASE_` prefix and
# refuses to deploy a .env declaring one.
FIRESTORE_DATABASE_ID=(default)

# ⚠️ THE ORIGIN AN EMAILED LINK IS BUILT AGAINST. The function is reached through a same-origin
# hosting rewrite, so it cannot tell which of the four allowed hosts it is running behind — an
# allowlist is not self-identification. A verify link cannot be relative, so this has to be stated.
#
# ⚠️ PROD'S FILE STAYS ABSENT, exactly as it does for FIRESTORE_DATABASE_ID. Without it the link
# builders return null and the caller REFUSES TO SEND, rather than emailing a hundred founding
# writers a URL that goes nowhere — a failure nobody discovers until someone clicks.
WAITLIST_PUBLIC_URL=https://scriptally-dev.web.app
